  "headline": "Charity Campaigner Claire Lomas Dies at 44",
  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner and inspirational figure, has died at the age of 44 following an accident in Jordan on 22 August. Lomas, who lived in Melton, Leicestershire, was left paralysed from the chest down after a horse-riding accident in 2007. Despite her injury, she raised nearly £1 million for charity and made headlines for completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days using a bionic suit and for lighting the Paralympic cauldron that same year. In 2016, she participated in the Great North Run while pregnant, completing it over five days in her bionic suit. Her family has expressed their devastation and requested privacy to grieve."
}
```

